WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
(steady pensive piano music)

00:00:05.247 --> 00:00:06.969
- [Voiceover] One of the
coolest things is when we take

00:00:06.969 --> 00:00:10.626
a diver with a disability in open water.

00:00:10.626 --> 00:00:15.212
The word freedom comes up
over and over and over again

00:00:15.212 --> 00:00:18.463
because that's how they
describe their feeling.

00:00:18.463 --> 00:00:22.198
(steady pensive piano music)

00:00:22.198 --> 00:00:25.321
My name's Jim Elliott, founder
and president of Diveheart.

00:00:25.321 --> 00:00:27.179
We help people with disabilities

00:00:27.179 --> 00:00:30.221
using zero gravity and scuba therapy.

00:00:30.221 --> 00:00:31.788
It's a great equalizer.

00:00:31.788 --> 00:00:35.155
We take their new normal, in some cases,

00:00:35.155 --> 00:00:37.210
and we help create a paradigm shift

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:39.149
so now the individual with the disability

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:41.649
isn't defined by that disability.

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:43.366
And they go into a room, and people say:

00:00:43.366 --> 00:00:44.199
"You do what?

00:00:44.199 --> 00:00:45.058
"You scuba dive?

00:00:45.058 --> 00:00:49.141
"That's impossible!
You're in a wheelchair."

00:00:49.141 --> 00:00:51.084
- [Jim] Tilt it back a little bit?

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.268
OK, guys, come up.

00:00:52.268 --> 00:00:55.182
- I was on my bicycle,
and I was struck by a car,

00:00:55.182 --> 00:00:59.907
and I hurt my T11 vertebrae
and severed my spinal cord.

00:00:59.907 --> 00:01:01.858
I knew that all of a sudden
when I lost the feeling

00:01:01.858 --> 00:01:06.850
and the ability to move my
legs that life had changed.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:10.008
- When I was 23 years
old, I dove into a pool

00:01:10.008 --> 00:01:13.433
and I dislocated my C67 vertebrae,

00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:16.637
which led me to be
paralyzed from my neck down.

00:01:16.637 --> 00:01:20.804
I'm totally dependent from
someone else all the time.

00:01:23.046 --> 00:01:25.728
I suffer from neurological pain,

00:01:25.728 --> 00:01:28.410
and I take medication for that,

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.952
but every time I get into
the water I feel better;

00:01:30.952 --> 00:01:35.119
I don't feel pain for a
couple of days, so I love it.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.564
- We see immediate pain relief.

00:01:41.564 --> 00:01:44.641
Individuals with everything
from MS to spinal-cord injuries

00:01:44.641 --> 00:01:47.974
and cerebral palsy can become pain-free.

00:01:49.006 --> 00:01:51.223
If we can get divers deep enough,

00:01:51.223 --> 00:01:53.615
to 66 feet, which is three atmospheres,

00:01:53.615 --> 00:01:56.657
there's an extra output of
serotonin in the human body.

00:01:56.657 --> 00:01:58.584
The serotonin will help
with the pain management

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.314
up to three weeks.

00:02:00.314 --> 00:02:02.462
It just helps their quality of life

00:02:02.462 --> 00:02:06.629
in so many different ways:
body, mind and spirit.

00:02:08.348 --> 00:02:10.775
- Diving is just amazing,
'cause I get outta this position

00:02:10.775 --> 00:02:12.307
and I can kinda do whatever I want

00:02:12.307 --> 00:02:13.828
and get in whatever position I want,

00:02:13.828 --> 00:02:16.521
which you don't get to do on land.

00:02:16.521 --> 00:02:18.077
When you're kinda stuck to a chair,

00:02:18.077 --> 00:02:21.827
being weightless is one
of the best feelings.

00:02:22.814 --> 00:02:24.579
- I was looking at myself standing up;

00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:26.587
and that was, for me, fabulous.

00:02:26.587 --> 00:02:27.420
I loved it.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.306
I was like: "Oh my god,

00:02:28.306 --> 00:02:30.779
"I cannot believe I'm seeing
myself standing up again!"

00:02:30.779 --> 00:02:32.253
After, imagine, so many years,

00:02:32.253 --> 00:02:35.597
15 years that I got my accident.

00:02:35.597 --> 00:02:38.464
I feel like totally independent
and I feel like freedom,

00:02:38.464 --> 00:02:40.484
liberty out of the power chair.

00:02:40.484 --> 00:02:41.651
It's me again.

